 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159348 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159348 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "406df982-fe24-53be-a818-6d89f4d6263e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159349 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159349 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159349 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4d498da2-7ca8-5ca1-82f1-71c24ce8e398" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186159351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186159352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186159353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186159354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159350 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186159355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159350 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159350 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159350 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a34b484a-c298-5baa-a88b-4834839a72f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159351 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159351 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159351 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a8f26b67-7bce-5dec-a9d2-5f72b8f032a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159352 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159352 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159352 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bb9f5b53-fbfb-54ce-bffc-2071f53d5073" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159353 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159353 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159353 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d830a714-4eae-5719-b96a-c7d0d54524f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159354 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159354 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159354 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e7ec41b0-e2f2-5424-80b4-200ea02084e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159355 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159355 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186159355 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "436bc0df-12a7-5c3b-a475-c1309eb76053" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161907 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161907 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample mean vector of $X$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161907 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5f949e10-0d73-50c8-9f41-73a0d0f78e29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161907 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the sample mean vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{m} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n \\mathbf{x}_i\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_1, \\mathbf{x}_2, \\ldots, \\mathbf{x}_n$ are the individual observations (columns of $X$).\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{1}{4}(x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3} + x_{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161908 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9834" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161908 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample covariance matrix of the data." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161908 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bd9fe016-cd5f-5e65-b388-35725ac0fbf4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161908 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC = \\dfrac{1}{n-1} B B^T\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations.\n\nSo, we first need to compute the mean-deviation form of our observation matrix.\n\nThe sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{1}{3}(x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}(\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb_{1} &= x_{1} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nb_{2} &= x_{2} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nb_{3} &= x_{3} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, the sample covariance matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nC &= \\frac{1}{3 - 1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 10 \\\\ 10 & 50\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161909 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9835" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161909 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 9 & 4 \\\\ 15 & -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161909 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bdef2fdc-0a38-5bfa-9bc6-7ca50e8c10ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186161909 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the mean-deviation form of the observation matrix\n\n$$\n[ \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid; x_{1}\\begin{vmatrix}x_{2} & ⋯\\end{vmatrix}x_{n}; \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid ]\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n$$\n[ \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid; b_{1}\\begin{vmatrix}b_{2} & ⋯\\end{vmatrix}b_{n}; \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid \\mid ]\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b}_i = \\mathbf{x}_i - \\mathbf{m}\n$$\n\nfor\n\n$$\ni = 1,2, \\ldots, n\n$$\n\nand $\\mathbf{m}$ is sample mean vector.\n\nFrom the matrix, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the sample mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{1}{3}(x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}(\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb_{1} &= x_{1} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nb_{2} &= x_{2} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nb_{3} &= x_{3} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean-deviation form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 12 & -10 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162094 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162094 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162094 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162094 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162094 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162094 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Sample Mean of an Observation Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162094 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186161907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162094 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "f930dfb2-a688-5dbe-9233-09dbcd2ba383" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050727 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186410431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Covariance Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186161908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162095 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "dc84d72a-b9f3-5f99-aa23-31cfe6910d49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162096 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162096 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186162358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162096 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Mean-Deviation Form of an Observation Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162096 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186161909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162096 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e91708c9-67e2-5228-84fd-1f4ea60064ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186163057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1045 "The Sample Covariance Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186163040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050911 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162232 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "d215dc31-fcec-5081-8994-43caf3b19295" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162353 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186159320 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162353 #edb/ref 1069 "q-137296" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162353 #edb/ref 1071 "$X = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162353 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "22493cd3-4d2e-5c66-bb31-313c49c59d2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162354 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186159326 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162354 #edb/ref 1069 "q-137297" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162354 #edb/ref 1071 "$B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the observation matrix $B$ in the mean-deviation form above, where the individual observations are given in columns.\nFind the sample covariance matrix of the data." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162354 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bfee1079-b365-5e37-895d-1b49cb096f78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162355 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186159332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162355 #edb/ref 1069 "q-137298" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162355 #edb/ref 1071 "$X = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -10 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample covariance matrix of the data." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162355 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd71fe61-2928-5f70-8006-22add51dc115" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162357 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186159344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162357 #edb/ref 1069 "q-138589" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162357 #edb/ref 1071 "$X = \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 8 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 10 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the sample mean vector of $X$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162357 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a8e04663-eff2-5470-8316-f5df1f548b39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162358 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186159350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162358 #edb/ref 1069 "q-138610" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162358 #edb/ref 1071 "$X = \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nConsider the observation matrix $X$ above, where the individual observations are given in columns. Find the mean-deviation form of $X$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162358 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a6f656ec-c43b-57fd-ba21-5aa8a0f97292" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163040 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186163041 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163040 #edb/ref 1061 36980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163040 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1e325102-149c-5fb3-b355-d46756b13060" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163040 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186163310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163041 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186163057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163041 #edb/ref 1061 36981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163041 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5ccead82-f536-5ecc-ad47-7e72852fc8a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163041 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162094 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163042 #edb/ref 1061 36982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163042 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b20cf4dd-9e6f-553b-bdb8-e16bac07f0be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163042 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162095 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163043 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186163042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163043 #edb/ref 1061 36983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163043 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f03f6d4f-4aba-584a-86ea-090a017828ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163043 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186163311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163044 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186163043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163044 #edb/ref 1061 36984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163044 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a74161b0-4fa2-5cab-a830-1e6a769934fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163044 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186162096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163057 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186163044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163057 #edb/ref 1061 37301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163057 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8e871f51-8d02-5990-9d6d-f5e78d503fb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163057 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186163321 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163310 #edb/ref 1064 "The table below describes the number of classes taken per semester and the average final grade in a sample of four college students.\n\n| **Number of Courses** | $4$ | $3$ | $5$ | $4$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| **Average Grade** | $80$ | $85$ | $75$ | $72$ |\n\nWe can collect this data in a matrix so that each column reports the number of courses and the average grade of a single student:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 80 & 85 & 75 & 72\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe matrix $X$ is called the **observation matrix.**\n\nSuppose we want to determine the mean number of courses and the mean average grade of this sample. The **sample mean vector,** denoted $\\mathbf m$, is a vector containing these values. The sample mean vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{m} = \\dfrac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n \\mathbf{x}_i\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_1, \\mathbf{x}_2, \\ldots, \\mathbf{x}_n$ are the individual observations (columns of $X$).\n\nFrom our matrix above, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sample mean vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm &= \\frac{1}{4}(x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3} + x_{4}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}(\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 85\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 75\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 72\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 312\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 78\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the average number of courses is $4$, and the average final grade is $78$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163310 #edb/ref 1065 6079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163310 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "652defa1-c802-5dbd-9ed9-7d863bd020a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163310 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163311 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider again the mean-deviation matrix for the students' data we found previously:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 7 & -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nCalculating the product $B B^T$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 7 & -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 98\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's analyze what we've obtained:\n\n- The entry in the first row and first column (${\\color{red}2}$) is the sum of the squares of the mean deviations of the number of courses.\n- The entry in the second row and second column (${\\color{blue}98}$) is the sum of the squares of the mean deviations of the final grades.\n- The off-diagonal entries (${\\color{purple}-10}$) are the sum of the products of the mean deviations.\n\nSince there were $4$ observations in total, if we divide each entry by $4-1=3$, we will get a matrix $C$ with the *sample variances* in the diagonal and the *sample covariance* in the off-diagonal positions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 98\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThis matrix is called the **covariance matrix** of the data.\n\nIn general, the sample covariance matrix is given by\n\n$$\nC = \\dfrac{1}{n-1} B B^T\n$$\n\nwhere $B$ is the observation matrix in the mean-deviation form, and $n$ is the number of observations." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163311 #edb/ref 1065 6080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163311 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "53d475a6-4449-56eb-8cf7-736ae440e1a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163311 #edb/ref 1067 "The Covariance Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163321 #edb/ref 1064 "Earlier, we studied data that reported the number of courses selected and the average grades of a sample of four college students. The observation matrix for this data was\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 80 & 85 & 75 & 72\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe individual observations are\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe also found the sample mean vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 78\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nOne thing we can do with this data is to check how much each observation differs from the mean values. To do that, we compute the difference between each observation and the sample mean vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb_{1} &= x_{1} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 78\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nb_{2} &= x_{2} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 85\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 78\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nb_{3} &= x_{3} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 75\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 78\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nb_{4} &= x_{4} - m = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 72\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 78\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe collect these differences in a new matrix, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 7 & -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe matrix $B$ is the **mean-deviation form** of $X$. It's often easier to work with the mean-deviation form, especially if the original data contains large numbers.\n\nNotice that the mean of a mean-deviation form equals the zero vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_{B} &= \\frac{1}{4}(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}(\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163321 #edb/ref 1065 6143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163321 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "fcfec935-52c3-571d-b471-9a1be7383ff6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186163321 #edb/ref 1067 "Mean-Deviation Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
